# Decisions

> This is your running log of the calls you have made and why. When you change your
> plan, drop an offer, pick a channel, or settle a question, jot it here so the
> reason is not lost. Newest goes on top. The system reads this to understand your
> thinking; you and the system both add to it over time.

_Add a new entry at the top. A date, what you decided, and the why in a line or two
is all it needs._

---

## Open decisions (kept current; review at the start of every DigiStart session)
Each line says who decides, and by when it is needed. When a line is decided, write the decision as a dated entry below, fill the `[PLACEHOLDER]` in the brain file that holds it, and delete the line here. Last updated 2026-10-14.

1. **Start date** (Wednesday 11 Nov or Wednesday 25 Nov) and the end of sign-up. Lenka and Štěpánka. The text of the page does **not** wait for it: the date stays a `[PLACEHOLDER: datum prvního setkání]` while the text is written. Lenka wants to see the two options as a calendar picture first and talk it over with Štěpánka. Placeholder in: business.md, plan.md, work/strategy/digistart-nabidka-pilot.md.
2. **Content of the four meetings**, first the two fixed ones, and whether the course includes building a website. Lenka. Needed by 30 Oct (campaign plan).
3. **Consultation before buying:** free or paid, 20 or 30 minutes. Lenka and Štěpánka.
4. **Payment:** at sign-up, or only after the decision to open; and what happens to the money if the course does not open (fewer than 10). Štěpánka.
5. **VAT** (price with or without), and a legal check that "no guarantee, no refund" fits the buyer's rights when buying online. GNOSTIKA as seller, or a lawyer.
6. **Will the course cost more after the pilot?** The words "pilotní cena" hint at it. Lenka.
7. **Fifth meeting:** will it be held? Later.
8. **What participants pay Anthropic for Claude**, and whether a paid plan is needed. To verify before the page is written (the price page and the vault note disagree).
9. **Štěpánka's voice.** Needed only when a text goes out in her name (her e-mails, her consultation invitation, posts from her profile). Štěpánka already built voice profiles in the test run, so one probably exists on her computer. Ask her for that profile file when the first such text is needed (check it for private details first). Also her consent to be quoted.
10. **Domain, Facebook page, pixel, ad account, spending cap, operator and terms on the page.** None exist yet. Only Lenka may confirm the ids for setup.md.
11. **Capacity:** cut the plan or move the dates, because 10 hours a week does not cover the campaign plan's estimate. Lenka.
12. **Selling from mid-November to Christmas:** Lenka does not want it, but the ads and a 25 Nov start sit in that window. Lenka, with item 1.

## 2026-10-14: the offer, changes after Lenka read the first draft
**Decided (Lenka, reading the offer in the queue):**
- The website is not a "wish". Lenka and Štěpánka built a page with AI and put it online. It is an example of what AI can do for solo businesswomen who struggle with sites that look poor and are hard to change. She does not want the offer to dwell on websites.
- Ads and the page do not narrow the audience to "podnikatelky": two women will attract other women too.
- The wording must not say "budeme zkoušet" (it sounds unsure). That participants influence what the next meetings cover is sold as a **benefit** of the pilot.
- DigiStart does not sell a ready-made system. It guides the women through building their own, step by step, instead of giving them a package to click through alone.
- The optional fifth meeting is in the price if it is held.
- **No guarantee and no refund**, because the meetings are live workshops.
**Why:** the first draft read flat and unsure, and wrongly called the website a wish.
**Open:** what happens to the payment if the course does not open; whether a no-refund line fits the buyer's legal rights (GNOSTIKA is the seller).

## 2026-10-14: plan changes after the first read
**Decided (Lenka, setup chat):** video stays in the plan as an ambition and is cut only if capacity does not allow. No e-mail sequences (no recruiting webinar is planned) and no other social networks. 20 participants is a flexible upper limit, not a cap. Lenka's 10 hours a week is her time only and can be moved to weekends; Štěpánka can also work on it; exact times are not committed because duration and the final look of each result are uncertain. Not selling from about the middle of November until Christmas, because it is the pre-Christmas season.
**Why:** the campaign plan is ambitious, so the plan is an ideal picture to cut down from or shift in time. Lenka's reason for not selling before Christmas: she and Štěpánka do not want to.

## 2026-10-14: the price is shown openly
**Decided (Lenka, with Štěpánka, said in the setup chat):** the price of 15 000 Kč is not hidden behind a consultation. Common sales advice says not to give the price in advance and to reveal it on a booked call. DigiStart will not use it.
**Why:** it does not fit them. They also see two likely effects: many women book the pre-sale call and few buy, or hiding the price puts women off so they never book. The tactic is probably tested on some other market.
**Also decided:** no puffed-up marketing words such as "revoluční" or "zázračné". The rule is about tone.

## 2026-10-14: what the opening message says
**Decided (Lenka, in the setup chat):** the message at the start of the ad and the page is about everyday needs of a small business owner, but one level above "use AI for your daily work". People already think of AI as something they ask for an e-mail, a plan, a text or a table, and then copy the answer around themselves. DigiStart shows the next step: AI can do the work itself. The wow is that it can build a website and put it online itself. This difference must be said right at the start.
**Why:** "Use AI for your daily work" is too little; participants already have that picture. The step up is AI working for the small business owner, not the owner working for AI.
**Open:** what exactly can be promised about the website (built by AI, put online by AI) needs a check against what the course really delivers before any ad says it. See [[audience]] and the offer once written.

## 2026-10-14: DigiStart set up as a third business
**Decided (Lenka, brief of 2026-10-14):** DigiStart gets its own business folder in GrowOS, with data kept apart from lcenglish and tadylenka. Strategy and `#next-action` stay in the vault project `projects/digistart.md`. Production is work items in `digistart/work/`. Facts in the brain come only from the sources the brief names. Nothing is written into `setup.md` as a channel id until Lenka confirms it; no id exists yet.
**Why:** the charter forbids mixing one business's facts or accounts into another. Meta accounts of LCEnglish are another business.
